# Trivy allowlist for accepted CVEs with no available fix.
#
# Trivy only matches a bare CVE ID per non-comment line — a line with extra
# text after the ID will not match anything, silently leaving the CVE
# blocked with no error. Entry format — a comment block explaining the
# acceptance, then the bare CVE ID on its own line:
#   # CVE-YYYY-NNNNN — <package> — <reason>
#   # No fix available as of <date>. Whether reachable in production.
#   # Remove when: <package> releases a patched version.
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN
#
# The PR adding an entry here must explain, in the PR description:
# - Which CVE is being accepted and what it is
# - Why no fix is currently available
# - Whether the vulnerable code path is reachable in production
# - A plan to remove the entry once a fix is released
#
# No entries currently — both frontend and backend images scan clean.
